{{also|huguenot}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|huguenot||Huguenot; also, a personal name and surname}}, diminutive of {{m|fr|Hugo}}, {{m|fr|Hugon}}, {{m|fr|Hugues}}, from {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{m|gmh|Hūg}}, {{m|gmh|Hūc||Hugh, a man's name}}, from {{etyl|gmh|en}} {{m|gmh|huge||mind}}, from {{etyl|goh|en}} {{m|goh|hugu||mind, thought}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*huguz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*hugiz||mind}}, of unknown origin. Cognate with {{cog|ang|hyge||thought, mind, heart, disposition, intention, courage, pride}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|hyū'gə-nŏt'}}, {{IPA|/ˈhju.ɡə.nɒt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} A [[member]] of the [[Protestant]] Reformed Church of [[France]] during the 16th and 17th [[century]].

